{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c5dfe32811af419bafdbaf0a71395f71f2788ce7dc9f2e0ce3adda26a5119039","digest":{"component_or_area":"GitHub workflow CI: build-and-test matrix","key_entities":[".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","jobs.test","jobs.lint","python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --lock","OS/Python test matrix"],"problem_keywords":["duplicate work","complexity baseline lock","workflow optimization","runner seconds","ci performance","redundant execution"],"propositions":["The complexity-baseline lock script runs four times per Verified change—once in each of Ubuntu 3.11/3.12/3.13 and macOS 3.12 test-matrix cells—despite being OS/Python-invariant and commit-level.","Moving the unchanged lock invocation from jobs.test matrix to the single jobs.lint job reduces duplicate fetch/merge-base work from ~154 runner-seconds per Verified run while preserving fail-closed policy and gate coverage.","A workflow unit oracle must enforce exactly one complexity-lock invocation in jobs.lint and prohibit it in the test matrix to prevent future duplicate placement.","The existing fail-closed and definition-vs-tree-skew behavior must remain unchanged after consolidation."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787910016264127001,"uuid":"80532118-0fa8-406f-b95f-78aeea4f09c2"}